//? Title: LL(1) predictive parsing
//? Subtitle: Actual FIRST/FOLLOW tables, original expressions and bounded stack decisions
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Predictive parsing expands a nonterminal using one lookahead token and an
indexed production table. We inspect actual native fixed-point sets, table
conflicts and stack actions, retain the original arithmetic grammar and
recognition controls, and separate syntax rejection from action-budget
exhaustion. Conflicted tables are diagnostic objects; parsing refuses them
rather than silently choosing a rule that can loop on left recursion.
)

\toc

> FIRST, FOLLOW and one lookahead

FIRST(alpha) contains terminals that can begin a derivation of alpha, plus
epsilon when it can vanish. FOLLOW(A) contains terminals that can follow
nonterminal A, with the native end marker in FOLLOW(start). For each indexed
production A→alpha, table(A,a) receives its rule ID for each terminal in
FIRST(alpha), and also each FOLLOW(A) member when alpha is nullable. A cell
encountering another rule ID records an actual conflict; the earliest rule
remains stored for inspection. Duplicate indexed productions can also conflict
even if deduplicating the mathematical grammar would remove that redundant
choice.

FIRST and FOLLOW are finite monotone set fixed points, not guesses from test
expressions. The native constructor counts their actual passes and successful
member insertions. No report-side grammar analysis rebuilds those sets or
predictive decisions. Epsilon is an empty rhs vector, not a literal empty-string
token; the dollar end marker is reserved for the parser.

> Tiny actual expansion and epsilon use

Use S→a*S*b | epsilon, which recognizes a^n*b^n. On a,a,b,b, the first expansion
pushes the reversed rhs so the first a is at the stack top. Later, lookahead b
chooses the epsilon rule without consuming a token. The complete native trace
exposes every actual before/after stack and chosen rule. Stack vectors are shown
bottom-to-top.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ll1_stack.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/ll1_parser.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const dm::algorithms::LL1Parser p({{{"S", {"a", "S", "b"}}, {"S", {}}}, "S"});
    auto t = p.trace({"a", "a", "b", "b"});
    std::print("| actual action index | actual input offset | actual top | actual lookahead | actual " "action0:expand,1:match,2:accept,3:reject | actual production or minus1 | actual stack " "after, bottom to top |\n| ---: | ---: | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (auto &e : t.events) {
        std::string stack;
        for (auto &s : e.after)
            stack += s + " ";
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", e.step,
                   e.input_offset, e.top, e.lookahead, int(e.action),
                   e.production, stack);
    }
    auto first = t.events.front();
    std::string stack;
    for (auto &s : first.after)
        stack += s + " ";
    auto epsilon =
        std::find_if(t.events.begin(), t.events.end(), [](const auto &e) {
        return e.production == 1;
    });
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("initial", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual stack top{}\nlookahead{}", first.top,
                       first.lookahead)).node("expanded", {6, 0},
                                              std::format(
                                              "Actual rule{} expansion\nstack{}",
                                              first.production, stack)).node(
        "epsilon", {12, 0},
        std::format("Actual epsilon rule{}\ninput offset{} unchanged",
                    epsilon->production, epsilon->input_offset)).edge("initial",
                                                                      "expanded").edge("expanded", "epsilon", "later actual action");
    d.save_svg("build/ll1_stack.svg");
}
```
